WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:11.490
In the Encyclopedia of Triangle Centers, X one is the Incenter: the point where the three interior angle bisectors of triangle A B C concur, and the center of its unique inscribed circle.

2
00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:25.734
Because X one is equidistant from sidelines B C, C A, and A B by the inradius r, its trilinear coordinates are simply one, to one, to one, while its barycentric sub-triangle areas scale directly with the side lengths, a, to b, to c.

3
00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:36.280
Toggle the central lines, and X one anchors the Nagel line through X two, X eight, and X ten, the Feuerbach line through X five and X eleven, and the Soddy line through X seven.

4
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:48.519
Under functional relations, X one is its own isogonal conjugate, the isotomic conjugate of X seventy-five, the anticomplement of the Spieker center X ten, and the complement of the Nagel point X eight.

5
00:00:48.519 --> 00:00:55.340
Across acute, right, Kepler, and Kimberling reference triangles, X one remains the invariant center of the incircle.
